  annotation "note_1771584212646_0", anchor: "extraordinary juridical significance or extraordinary juridical confusion", text: "Meant both. The Foedus∴vincu alone has been rewritten after five separate conflicts. An artifact central to five governing instruments is either a constitutional keystone or evidence that Nightshelf governance is five contradictory oaths that happen to reference the same object. I have catalogued enough Nightshelf administrative ice to suspect the latter, but I admire the ambiguity.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771584212646_1", anchor: "an era whose artifacts I have learned to approach with particular caution", text: "Clever Ice Age provenance is claimed more often than it can be verified. The deep ice under Aurora Stack contains at least three artifacts dated to that era whose pressure-signatures place them centuries later. I am not saying this is one of them. I am saying I have no independent method to confirm it isn't, and neither does anyone else still working down here.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771584212646_2", anchor: "luminous ink — pale blue-green, the color of bioluminescence — that reveals itself only in perfect darkness", text: "Not perfect darkness. Near-perfect. Nightshelf shadow-readers use controlled absence — aurora-crystal light reduced to its final decay-flicker, then extinguished. The ink responds to the transition, not the state. This distinction matters for anyone attempting to read the grimoire by simply sitting in a dark cave, which I am told at least two Aurora scholars have tried.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771584212646_3", anchor: "Three keepers lost to madness, silence, or death before the tome reached anyone capable of using it", text: "Nightshelf oral tradition names five pre-Sivruta~ bearers, not three. Two are omitted because they held the tome less than a full dark-cycle — brief enough that most accounts round them away. I let the cleaner number stand in the main text because it serves the pattern I was drawing. I am aware of what that makes me.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771584212646_4", anchor: "her flipper froze permanently in the shape of gripping the tome's weight", text: "The shape of gripping something that is no longer there. Mine is across the left flipper, not the right, and the cause was ice rather than fire, but the body remembers the weight of what it held at the moment everything changed. The Nightshelf sent a formal apology for what happened in the Whisper Galleries. I should probably open it one of these years.", type: :tangent, display: :full
